  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1933\n£10.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nCompiled and Edited by THE CHRONICLE EDITORIAL COMMITTEE\n\nVolume XLI\n\nJanuary to December 1933\n\nPublished 1934 - Slatter & Rose Oxford. Hardcover.\n\n252 pages\n\nContents:\n\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Calendat for 1933\n\nThe Army List, December 1933\n\nOfficers of The Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed, December 31st, 1933\n\nFormer Officers of The Regiment Now Serving in the Royal Air Force, December 31st, 1933\n\nFormer Officers of The Regiment on the Active List of the Army, December 31st, 1933\n\nFormer Officers of The Regiment Belonging to the Reserve of Officers, December 31st, 1933\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette', 1933\n\nRecords of the First Battalion\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary\n\nFirst Battalion Letter, 1933\n\nRecords of the Second Battalion\n\nSummary of the Second Battalion Diary\n\nSecond Battalion Letter, 1933\n\nRecords of the Depot\n\nDepot Letter, 1933\n\nThe Regimental Dinner, 1933\n\n43rd (Provisional Battalion) Dinner\n\nWeapon Training, 1933\n\nSignalling, 1933\n\nAthletics, 1933\n\nCricket, 1933\n\nFootball, 1933\n\nHockey, 1933\n\nBoxing, 1933\n\nPolo, 1933\n\nRacing in Burma, 1933\n\nShooting in Burma, 1933\n\nThe Regimental Race, 1933\n\nHunting\n\nThe Booth Letters (Concluded)\n\nThe 43rd Powder Horn\n\nThe Rangoon Searchlight Tattoo, 1933\n\nThe Andamans, 1933\n\nSome Peninsular Battlefields\n\nWith the Amateur Athletic Association in Holland, Finland and Italy\n\nThe Regimental Committee\n\nOld Comrades Association\n\nEnsign Pocklington\n\n43rd Army List, 1854 - 55\n\n52nd Army List, 1854 - 55\n\nWith the 52nd to India in 1853\n\nObituary\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre VII\n£5.00 Add to cart\nWinston Churchill: Oxfordshire Hussar – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\nThe Story of the Oxfordshire Yeomanry – Queen’s Own Oxfordshire Hussars 1798-1998\n£7.95 Read more\nRedcoats to Riflemen: A Short History of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire County Regiment\n£4.50 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
